WEBVTT

00:00.114 --> 00:03.470
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:03.505 --> 00:06.740
♪ Is violence in
movies and sex on TV ♪

00:06.775 --> 00:10.610
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.645 --> 00:13.546
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.582 --> 00:16.883
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:16.918 --> 00:20.220
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.255 --> 00:22.085
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.116 --> 00:23.413
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.452 --> 00:28.762
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:33.976 --> 00:36.710
We now return to The Terminator.

00:38.480 --> 00:40.213
I've been sent here from the future.

00:40.249 --> 00:43.183
I have to have sex with your
housekeeper to save humanity.

00:43.218 --> 00:44.217
What?

00:44.253 --> 00:45.552
Bring me your housekeeper!

00:45.587 --> 00:47.287
I have to have sex with her now!

00:47.322 --> 00:48.688
I'm the Terminator!

00:48.724 --> 00:49.990
I don't have a housekeeper.

00:50.025 --> 00:51.124
And I think you're just

00:51.160 --> 00:52.759
present-day Arnold Schwarzenegger.

00:52.795 --> 00:54.394
No, I am a machine.

00:54.430 --> 00:57.364
Every second I'm not having
sex with a housekeeper,

00:57.399 --> 01:00.133
robots are killing people in the future.

01:00.169 --> 01:02.135
Okay, I finish for the day.

01:02.171 --> 01:03.403
You lied to me!

01:03.439 --> 01:04.971
You do have a housekeeper!

01:05.007 --> 01:07.648
Let's go make a large-faced boy.

01:09.945 --> 01:11.611
Whoa, whoa, whoa, cop, cop, cop.

01:11.647 --> 01:14.514
Peter, it's me, and you're an
adult man drinking in a bar.

01:14.550 --> 01:15.882
Anyway, sorry I'm late.

01:15.918 --> 01:18.351
The pantry down at the
station needed new shelf paper.

01:18.387 --> 01:20.053
That's what they got
you doing down there?

01:20.088 --> 01:22.456
Well, that, and I'm also in
charge of the office gerbil.

01:22.491 --> 01:25.625
And let me tell you, Lieutenant
Nibbles is quite a handful.

01:25.661 --> 01:27.928
He'll only eat real
cheese, not processed.

01:27.963 --> 01:30.230
You buy special cheese for a gerbil?

01:30.265 --> 01:32.065
Yeah, I have to, he outranks me.

01:32.100 --> 01:33.700
Jeez, Joe, what the hell happened?

01:33.735 --> 01:36.169
You used to be this badass
cop out there on the street,

01:36.205 --> 01:38.205
busting heads and keeping us safe.

01:38.240 --> 01:41.374
Well, it may not sound exciting,
but I play an important role.

01:41.410 --> 01:43.109
I go through all the body cam footage

01:43.145 --> 01:45.679
and take out all the parts
where the cops go pee-pee.

01:45.714 --> 01:48.582
So you're just erasing
cop wieners all day?

01:48.617 --> 01:50.750
Eh, not erasing, sort
of cutting them together

01:50.786 --> 01:53.019
into a funny montage
we show on birthdays.

01:53.055 --> 01:55.555
Speaking of which, Flannigan's
got the big "four-oh" coming up.

01:55.591 --> 01:56.590
Got to go.

01:57.791 --> 02:00.460
Man, you guys think Joe's
as happy as he says he is,

02:00.496 --> 02:02.329
just doing all that desk work?

02:02.364 --> 02:05.332
No way, he's just
putting lipstick on a pig.

02:05.367 --> 02:06.967
This is called "Crimson Sky."

02:07.002 --> 02:08.134
What do you think?

02:08.170 --> 02:09.302
Mmm.

02:09.338 --> 02:10.437
Harold?

02:10.472 --> 02:11.605
Get this off of me!

02:11.640 --> 02:13.507
What are you doing in
the women's department?

02:13.542 --> 02:15.141
Uh, waiting for you.

02:15.177 --> 02:16.843
Well, I'm ready. Let's go.

02:18.847 --> 02:21.202
Who are you?

02:27.022 --> 02:29.990
Ugh, she just put her
tampons on top of the bread.

02:30.025 --> 02:32.292
Take the groceries
out, we got start over.

02:32.327 --> 02:35.495
Mom, can I go barehand
raisins from the bulk aisle?

02:35.531 --> 02:36.730
Okay, but if you get caught,

02:36.765 --> 02:39.266
just say, "oopsie-poopsie,"
like a simpleton.

02:40.235 --> 02:41.968
Hey, watch your fat arms!

02:42.004 --> 02:44.638
Excuse me, ma'am, your little
girl dropped her teddy bear.

02:44.673 --> 02:45.639
What?

02:45.674 --> 02:47.107
"Little girl"?

02:48.243 --> 02:50.043
Yeah, she hates it when she drops that.

02:50.078 --> 02:53.113
He's actually a little boy,
but thank you very much.

02:53.148 --> 02:54.814
Did she just think I was a girl?

02:54.850 --> 02:56.316
Why would she think that?

02:56.351 --> 02:58.285
I don't know, maybe she saw
you try to throw that feather

02:58.287 --> 02:59.553
in the yard yesterday.

02:59.588 --> 03:01.856
Hey, don't watch me
when I'm doing stuff.

03:01.859 --> 03:03.223
What are you doing, kid?

03:03.225 --> 03:04.190
Those aren't free!

03:04.226 --> 03:06.192
Oopsie-poopsie!

03:06.228 --> 03:07.861
Aw, God bless you.

03:07.896 --> 03:09.663
Help yourself.

03:20.008 --> 03:20.974
Car trouble?

03:21.009 --> 03:22.208
Ah, son of a bitch, Joe!

03:22.244 --> 03:23.364
Didn't even hear you coming.

03:23.378 --> 03:25.946
Yeah, I'm kind of quiet on grass.

03:28.884 --> 03:30.517
Thanks for giving me a ride, Joe.

03:30.552 --> 03:32.085
Hey, since we're in a cop car,

03:32.120 --> 03:34.560
let's talk about our hunches
and how something doesn't add up.

03:34.590 --> 03:35.655
All right.

03:35.691 --> 03:38.491
I have a hunch Madea's
not really a girl.

03:38.527 --> 03:40.594
Yeah, something doesn't
add up about that.

03:40.629 --> 03:41.962
All units,

03:41.997 --> 03:44.230
reports of a drug deal in
progress at Fifth and Maple.

03:44.266 --> 03:45.231
Shots fired.

03:45.267 --> 03:46.866
Suspect possibly armed.

03:46.902 --> 03:50.036
Well, shots fired, so
definitely armed, duh.

03:50.072 --> 03:51.204
Dispatch much?

03:51.239 --> 03:52.672
Sorry, guys.

03:52.708 --> 03:54.074
Fifth and Maple? That's right near here.

03:54.076 --> 03:55.141
We got to go!

03:55.177 --> 03:56.876
No can do, I got to go to the station

03:56.912 --> 03:58.745
and tidy up the bulletin board.

03:58.780 --> 04:00.447
No one's biting on those guitar lessons.

04:00.482 --> 04:01.581
What are you talking about?

04:01.617 --> 04:03.216
There's a drug deal going down!

04:03.251 --> 04:06.019
Peter, there's a lot you don't
understand about police work.

04:06.054 --> 04:07.921
What's to understand? I watch TV.

04:07.956 --> 04:11.048
Come on, Joe, let's put this
70's siren on your car and go.

04:12.327 --> 04:14.294
Did you just wipe a booger on my roof?

04:14.329 --> 04:15.895
Let's go! Let's go!

04:18.775 --> 04:21.468
Oh, crap! Cops!

04:21.503 --> 04:22.502
That's the house!

04:24.106 --> 04:25.739
Hold on, Peter, we can't go in there.

04:25.774 --> 04:27.007
We got to wait for backup.

04:27.042 --> 04:28.775
The hell we do!

04:28.810 --> 04:30.176
Peter!

04:30.212 --> 04:32.012
Reach for the stars!

04:32.047 --> 04:33.054
What?

04:33.057 --> 04:35.324
I think he's telling
us to follow our dreams.

04:35.327 --> 04:36.293
Where are the drugs?

04:36.296 --> 04:37.362
What are you doing?

04:37.365 --> 04:39.753
You are violating all
kinds of procedures!

04:39.788 --> 04:41.554
There's no drugs here, pig.

04:44.493 --> 04:46.292
Ah-ha! No drugs, huh?

04:46.328 --> 04:47.694
Well, what do you call this?

04:47.729 --> 04:49.195
And I'll bet there's
more where that came from.

04:50.265 --> 04:52.365
They're trying to flush their stash!

04:53.468 --> 04:54.801
Nice try, scumbag,

04:54.836 --> 04:57.019
but I got your squishy drugs right here.

04:57.022 --> 04:58.104
Uh-oh.

04:58.140 --> 05:00.140
Peter, hand me my gun
and get out of here!

05:00.142 --> 05:01.641
I could get fired for this!

05:01.677 --> 05:05.412
And I can't go back to my
job as a magician's assistant.

05:07.616 --> 05:10.283
And now, to pull the two sides apart.

05:12.372 --> 05:14.572
And wiggle your toes!

05:15.576 --> 05:18.291
I said, wiggle your toes!

05:18.326 --> 05:19.693
Yeah, that's, uh,

05:19.728 --> 05:22.862
that's why I wanted to
talk to you before the show.

05:27.736 --> 05:28.935
What's up, dudes?

05:28.970 --> 05:30.370
Stewie, what the hell is all this?

05:30.405 --> 05:32.772
Uh, only the most manly thing ever.

05:32.808 --> 05:35.875
A little something
called American football.

05:35.911 --> 05:37.744
Is that a Michael Sam jersey?

05:37.779 --> 05:39.279
Yep. Two boy names.

05:39.314 --> 05:40.714
Doubly masculine.

05:40.749 --> 05:42.148
- Like George Michael?
- Shut up!

05:42.184 --> 05:44.017
Come on, Stewie, are
you still hung up about

05:44.052 --> 05:46.292
that woman at the grocery
store thinking you were a girl?

05:46.321 --> 05:47.587
Elton John.

05:47.622 --> 05:48.621
Is another.

05:48.657 --> 05:50.256
It has nothing to do with that, Brian.

05:50.292 --> 05:52.625
I just thought it'd be
good to take up a sport.

05:52.661 --> 05:54.094
You know, like boys do.

05:54.129 --> 05:56.362
You don't have to play
football to prove you're a boy.

05:56.398 --> 05:57.797
Barney Frank.

05:57.833 --> 05:59.632
Is yet another one.

05:59.668 --> 06:00.667
Chris, please.

06:00.702 --> 06:01.701
Actually, you know what? Ricky Martin.

06:01.703 --> 06:03.002
There's a bunch of these.

06:03.038 --> 06:04.637
Anyway, they're not gonna
let you play football, Stewie.

06:04.639 --> 06:05.605
You're too little.

06:05.640 --> 06:06.840
Oh, don't worry.

06:06.875 --> 06:08.875
I'm gonna be bad news
for the other team.

06:08.910 --> 06:11.144
And nobody likes bad news.

06:11.179 --> 06:14.180
Except for Larry, the
Self-Loathing Idiot.

06:14.216 --> 06:17.517
Larry, I'm afraid you only
have three months to live.

06:23.959 --> 06:25.692
Swanson!

06:25.727 --> 06:27.861
I need to see you right now!

06:30.165 --> 06:31.564
Captain.

06:31.600 --> 06:32.799
Lieutenant.

06:32.834 --> 06:35.201
You had no business
participating in that raid

06:35.237 --> 06:36.603
at Fifth and Maple.

06:36.638 --> 06:38.238
I know that, Captain.
I'm sorry that I...

06:38.273 --> 06:39.506
But I'm glad you did.

06:39.541 --> 06:40.940
Excuse me?

06:40.976 --> 06:43.676
You brought down one of the
biggest drug rings in Quahog.

06:43.712 --> 06:45.712
Above and beyond, Swanson.

06:45.747 --> 06:47.347
Well, sir, I...

06:47.382 --> 06:49.149
I'm just like any other cop.

06:49.184 --> 06:51.618
My wife puts on my
pants one leg at a time.

06:51.653 --> 06:53.920
I appreciate your
modesty, but nice work.

06:53.955 --> 06:56.222
It's hard to believe you
did that all by yourself.

06:56.258 --> 06:59.492
Yep, did it all by myself, I did, I did.

06:59.528 --> 07:02.495
My little lonesome, says I.

07:02.531 --> 07:04.731
That's weird phrasing, but
I'll tell you this, Swanson,

07:04.766 --> 07:06.166
you keep up this kind of work,

07:06.201 --> 07:08.201
there'll be no more
grocery runs for you.

07:08.236 --> 07:10.203
You'll be back on the street full-time.

07:10.238 --> 07:11.504
Thank you, Captain.

07:11.540 --> 07:13.773
Sir?

07:13.809 --> 07:15.096
Thank you, sir.

07:22.369 --> 07:23.602
Hey, Peter.

07:23.637 --> 07:26.071
You know, I was just thinking
about how much fun we had

07:26.106 --> 07:28.340
the other day, and wondered
if you'd want to join me

07:28.375 --> 07:29.908
for another ride-along.

07:29.943 --> 07:32.177
Well, yeah, but I-I thought
you said I couldn't do that

07:32.212 --> 07:33.378
'cause you'd get in trouble.

07:33.414 --> 07:34.880
Eh, it'll be our little secret.

07:34.915 --> 07:35.914
All right.

07:35.949 --> 07:37.149
Hey, can I drive the car?

07:37.184 --> 07:39.084
- Yeah, I guess I can let you drive.
- Awesome!

07:39.119 --> 07:41.353
Hey, and-and can we go
slow up to a homeless guy

07:41.388 --> 07:43.321
and go "joop-joop"
and see what he does?

07:43.357 --> 07:44.489
That's half the job.

07:44.525 --> 07:46.224
So, what do you say? You
think you're up to it?

07:46.226 --> 07:47.292
You bet I am.

07:47.327 --> 07:48.927
I'm in the best shape of my life.

07:48.962 --> 07:51.763
I've been working my Dave
Matthews Punching Bag.

07:51.799 --> 07:53.698
Thank you very much for using me today.

07:56.403 --> 07:57.969
This isn't annoying enough.

07:58.005 --> 07:59.572
I need my David Lee Roth bag.

08:09.616 --> 08:12.884
Wow. So these are the
wife-beaters of tomorrow.

08:12.920 --> 08:14.653
Which team is Stewie gonna be on?

08:14.688 --> 08:16.154
He's not gonna be on any team.

08:16.190 --> 08:18.957
He's just overcompensating,
because he was called a girl.

08:18.992 --> 08:21.660
But once he sees how big the
other kids are, he'll back out.

08:22.629 --> 08:24.696
Ooh! My shoes have 12 little heels.

08:24.731 --> 08:25.797
They're cleats!

08:25.833 --> 08:28.166
Okay, kids, let's start practice.

08:28.202 --> 08:29.367
Yeah! Football!

08:29.403 --> 08:31.036
Boy stuff. Hitting the shower.

08:31.071 --> 08:32.170
Getting embarrassed.

08:32.206 --> 08:33.271
Going home to shower.

08:33.307 --> 08:34.773
Okay, Stewie, enough is enough.

08:34.808 --> 08:36.508
All right, let's-let's
get you out of here.

08:36.543 --> 08:38.383
Yeah, you probably should
get him out of there,

08:38.412 --> 08:39.945
'cause he's just a little shrimp.

08:39.980 --> 08:41.580
Uh, okay, thank you.

08:41.615 --> 08:42.714
I mean, look at him.

08:42.749 --> 08:44.549
My Tyler would kill him out there.

08:44.585 --> 08:45.917
Okay, well, believe me, there's

08:45.953 --> 08:47.118
there's more to him than you think.

08:47.120 --> 08:48.086
Come on, Stewie.

08:48.121 --> 08:49.888
You know, ballet is great exercise.

08:49.923 --> 08:52.390
Maybe you should put
short stack in a tutu.

08:52.426 --> 08:53.625
No, you know what, Stewie?

08:53.660 --> 08:55.193
Get the hell out on that field!

08:55.229 --> 08:57.462
And if you see that
Tyler, take his knee out.

08:57.498 --> 08:58.497
All right, let's do it!

08:58.532 --> 08:59.531
Football game!

08:59.566 --> 09:02.133
Then, reminder, showering at home.

09:02.169 --> 09:05.170
Okay, I guess we'll see who's
got the toughest kid here.

09:05.205 --> 09:06.638
Yeah, I guess we will.

09:09.042 --> 09:10.008
Hey!

09:10.043 --> 09:12.077
Oopsie-poopsie!

09:12.112 --> 09:13.478
Aw.

10:26.019 --> 10:27.319
Good evening, I'm Tom Tucker.

10:27.354 --> 10:28.787
Our top story tonight:

10:28.822 --> 10:30.488
local news anchor too professional

10:30.524 --> 10:33.258
to laugh at penis poked
through hole in cue card.

10:33.293 --> 10:35.727
But first, earlier today at city hall,

10:35.762 --> 10:37.495
the mayor honored a hero cop

10:37.531 --> 10:39.998
who has foiled a
string of recent crimes.

10:40.033 --> 10:42.968
Good afternoon, we had a
budget meeting that ran long,

10:43.003 --> 10:44.769
so I'm gonna eat my lunch

10:44.805 --> 10:48.073
while I hold this press conference.

10:48.108 --> 10:49.941
Ooh, my favorite!

10:49.977 --> 10:52.711
Loose Cobb salad in a lunchbox.

10:52.746 --> 10:55.046
I'm gonna now shake this up

10:55.082 --> 10:58.550
like a lady in your office.

10:58.585 --> 11:01.286
Okay, while the dressing does its magic,

11:01.321 --> 11:03.822
let's honor Officer Joe Swanson,

11:03.857 --> 11:08.526
who single-handedly cut
crime in Quahog by 75%.

11:09.930 --> 11:12.230
What? "Single-handedly"?

11:12.265 --> 11:15.667
Officer Swanson, as thanks
from a grateful city,

11:15.702 --> 11:18.203
please accept this Certificate of Merit.

11:18.238 --> 11:23.108
And with that, I hereby
declare this hero cop open!

11:23.143 --> 11:25.076
Whoa, sweet bod.

11:25.112 --> 11:26.711
You lift, bro?

11:26.747 --> 11:29.214
Damn it, I can't believe
Joe's hogging all the credit.

11:29.249 --> 11:32.050
That bastard's just getting
famous by tricking people.

11:32.085 --> 11:33.785
Like Orson Welles.

11:33.820 --> 11:36.488
So the aliens have come to Earth

11:36.523 --> 11:38.923
to destroy all mankind.

11:38.959 --> 11:41.192
And, uh...

11:41.228 --> 11:43.395
they're going to start at McDonald's.

11:43.430 --> 11:46.798
So if you're in line
there, you better run.

11:46.833 --> 11:49.100
Whoa, whoa! N-Not the workers, though.

11:49.136 --> 11:52.070
They've already said
the workers are safe.

11:55.108 --> 11:59.477
Excuse me, Coach
Herar-Herar-ra-ra-ra...?

11:59.513 --> 12:00.645
It's Herrera.

12:00.681 --> 12:02.313
Okay, well that's a
lot of Rs, but listen,

12:02.315 --> 12:04.082
I-I noticed you're not starting Stewie.

12:04.117 --> 12:05.517
Oh, I can't put him in.

12:05.552 --> 12:07.152
I mean, he can come
out for limp handshakes

12:07.154 --> 12:09.721
at the end of the game, but I
can't play him. He's too little.

12:09.724 --> 12:10.588
"Little"?

12:10.624 --> 12:12.424
Oh, like that car you drive over there?

12:12.459 --> 12:15.460
Let's see if it looks bigger
when I throw a Sprite at it.

12:16.963 --> 12:19.330
Well, that's not my
car, but I don't care,

12:19.366 --> 12:21.099
I'm just a volunteer.

12:21.134 --> 12:22.667
All right, Griffin, get in there!

12:26.373 --> 12:29.340
Come on, Stewie, give your dog
something to post on Facebook!

12:29.376 --> 12:31.443
Something to post on Facebook, let's go.

12:34.781 --> 12:36.648
All right, and nobody's blocking.

12:39.119 --> 12:40.518
Oh, my God. Stewie!

12:41.488 --> 12:42.921
Are you okay?

12:42.956 --> 12:44.656
Back off! He may have a concussion.

12:44.691 --> 12:45.757
A concussion?

12:45.792 --> 12:47.926
You do me an honor, Lieutenant,

12:47.961 --> 12:51.262
but my dance card is full.

12:55.902 --> 12:57.802
Officer Swanson, as you requested,

12:57.838 --> 12:59.971
here's a big stack of
all the cases you cracked.

13:00.006 --> 13:02.841
Oh, great. Now I'm gonna go
ahead and brood over a photo

13:02.876 --> 13:06.478
of the girl whose case was
the one I couldn't solve.

13:06.513 --> 13:09.414
Your '70s sweater and
feathered hair let people know

13:09.449 --> 13:11.816
this is a cold case.

13:11.852 --> 13:14.819
Well, hello, Officer Swanson.

13:14.855 --> 13:16.554
Peter? What are you doing?

13:16.590 --> 13:18.223
You're not supposed to be here.

13:18.258 --> 13:21.826
I saw you on TV, hogging all
the credit for my police work.

13:21.862 --> 13:24.629
Look, I told you, I need you
to be a silent partner on this.

13:24.664 --> 13:26.831
The truth is I could
get in a lot of trouble.

13:26.867 --> 13:30.034
Oh, I see. You need me to be
the bad cop who kicks all the ass

13:30.070 --> 13:31.936
and then I'm supposed
to be quiet about it?

13:31.972 --> 13:34.372
Well, my silence is gonna cost you.

13:34.407 --> 13:35.440
What are you saying?

13:35.475 --> 13:37.675
I'm saying you get stuff, I want stuff.

13:37.711 --> 13:39.144
I've seen that evidence locker.

13:39.179 --> 13:41.045
I know you got Discmans in there.

13:41.081 --> 13:43.014
I want a murdered jogger's Discman.

13:43.049 --> 13:44.749
Peter, you know I can't do that.

13:44.785 --> 13:47.285
Yeah? Well, maybe I accidentally reveal

13:47.320 --> 13:49.320
that you're not the hero
everyone thinks you are

13:49.356 --> 13:50.722
and that you've been
letting your neighbor

13:50.724 --> 13:52.357
do all kinds of cop stuff.

13:52.392 --> 13:54.225
You wouldn't do that, would you?

13:54.261 --> 13:55.493
You bet I would.

13:55.529 --> 13:57.695
And one more thing.

13:57.731 --> 13:59.097
Peter asked me to do this.

13:59.132 --> 14:00.899
He, he said it's something from before.

14:00.934 --> 14:02.921
I, I don't know, I... I hope it's funny.

14:09.487 --> 14:12.557
All right, I'm here. But why
did you want me to bring this?

14:12.604 --> 14:14.751
I'll tell you why. You're
getting all the credit

14:14.786 --> 14:17.320
for my police work, so
I want stuff from you.

14:17.355 --> 14:19.589
I want a minute in your
house with this shopping cart,

14:19.624 --> 14:20.957
like Supermarket Sweep.

14:20.992 --> 14:22.258
Here, time me.

14:22.294 --> 14:25.128
Peter, you expect me to
let you ransack my house?

14:25.163 --> 14:27.597
Well, unless you'd rather I
spill the beans to the chief

14:27.632 --> 14:30.066
about who's been doing your dirty work.

14:30.101 --> 14:32.001
Okay, go.

14:34.005 --> 14:35.838
Aw, sweet, board games!

14:35.874 --> 14:37.666
I'm taking the cannon
from your Monopoly!

14:37.669 --> 14:39.976
Why is Peter in the house?

14:40.011 --> 14:42.078
It's a police matter, Bonnie!

14:42.113 --> 14:44.247
Hey, how come Kevin's room is locked?

14:44.282 --> 14:45.882
He just wants some privacy!

14:45.917 --> 14:47.617
It's locked from the outside!

14:47.652 --> 14:49.385
Don't open it, Peter!

14:51.022 --> 14:53.289
Hi, baby. Hi, baby.

14:53.325 --> 14:54.891
Get out of Susie's room!

14:57.028 --> 15:00.063
Your stuff sucks. I didn't
need the full minute.

15:04.028 --> 15:07.363
Hey, Stewie, how's our
little concussion guy?

15:10.141 --> 15:12.608
Oh, my God. Can you, can you see me?

15:12.644 --> 15:14.711
Yeah, I know, I'm fine, I'm fine.

15:14.746 --> 15:17.246
I-Is anybody gonna
answer that telephone?

15:17.282 --> 15:19.749
He keeps thinking the
phone is ringing, Brian.

15:19.784 --> 15:21.217
Well, at least he's talking again.

15:21.252 --> 15:22.652
I think that means he's getting better.

15:22.654 --> 15:24.454
Is it day or night?

15:24.489 --> 15:26.456
I don't, I don't care,
I just want to know.

15:26.491 --> 15:27.957
Lois, answer the bloody phone!

15:27.993 --> 15:29.759
N-No, no! W-we don't need Lois.

15:29.794 --> 15:31.461
Chris, pretend to answer the phone.

15:31.496 --> 15:33.329
Oh, uh, hello?

15:33.365 --> 15:35.698
Okay. Yes, one second.

15:35.734 --> 15:37.600
Mom, it's for you!

15:37.635 --> 15:39.035
What? No! Damn it, Chris!

15:39.070 --> 15:40.737
Um, um... I'll, I'll take that.

15:40.772 --> 15:42.672
Hello, this is Brian Griffin.

15:42.707 --> 15:45.274
Actually, I already
receive The New York Times,

15:45.310 --> 15:48.544
and I always enjoy finishing
the crossword puzzle.

15:48.580 --> 15:50.513
You're bragging to nobody?

15:50.548 --> 15:51.848
Phone's still ringing.

15:51.883 --> 15:53.683
Crap, Chris, he's worse
off than I thought.

15:53.718 --> 15:55.018
We have to do something.

15:55.053 --> 15:57.220
Well, on TV if somebody
gets hit on the head,

15:57.255 --> 16:00.690
you hit them a second time and
that gets them back to normal.

16:00.725 --> 16:02.258
No, no, Chris. This is very serious.

16:02.293 --> 16:05.161
You see, what a concussion is
is the impact of brain matter

16:05.196 --> 16:06.929
on the inside of the skull.

16:06.965 --> 16:08.925
That's why you sometimes
hear this nonsense about,

16:08.933 --> 16:10.500
"Oh, let's just give
them better helmets."

16:10.502 --> 16:13.236
But you can't make a
helmet for the inside...

16:13.271 --> 16:14.737
Chris, are you crazy?

16:14.773 --> 16:17.907
Shh. Let's just let him sleep this off.

16:17.942 --> 16:19.742
Look how peaceful he is.

16:19.778 --> 16:22.545
I wonder what's going on
in that little head of his.

16:25.116 --> 16:28.284
♪ The world looks
mighty good to me ♪

16:28.319 --> 16:31.821
♪ 'Cause Tootsie
Rolls are all I see ♪

16:31.856 --> 16:35.058
♪ Whatever it is I think I see ♪

16:35.093 --> 16:39.195
♪ Becomes a Tootsie Roll to me! ♪

16:43.334 --> 16:45.668
Joe, is something wrong?

16:45.703 --> 16:48.805
I didn't hear you crying
in the shower this morning.

16:48.840 --> 16:50.840
I'm just dealing with
some stuff at work.

16:50.875 --> 16:52.809
But everything's going so well.

16:52.844 --> 16:54.677
You've been getting
all those commendations

16:54.712 --> 16:58.648
and my online handmade lip balm
business is really taking off.

16:58.683 --> 17:00.403
I don't even know what
you're talking about.

17:00.418 --> 17:02.118
Well, I'm proud of you.

17:02.153 --> 17:05.221
And you should be proud of yourself.

17:08.193 --> 17:10.660
I want these: rechargeable
heated mittens.

17:10.695 --> 17:12.728
Write it down.

17:12.764 --> 17:14.063
Forget it, Peter.

17:14.099 --> 17:15.598
I'm done being blackmailed by you.

17:15.633 --> 17:16.766
Oh, yeah?

17:16.801 --> 17:18.034
Well, fine, but remember,

17:18.076 --> 17:19.771
you're nothing without your muscle.

17:19.774 --> 17:21.304
Any available unit,

17:21.339 --> 17:24.340
we have a report of an
armed robbery in progress.

17:24.375 --> 17:26.809
Go on, hero cop. You don't need me.

17:26.845 --> 17:30.913
Well, uh, maybe you and
I could do one last bust

17:30.949 --> 17:32.215
for old time's sake.

17:32.250 --> 17:34.183
Yes! All right, let's do
it. Let's go be heroes.

17:34.219 --> 17:36.219
Like the designated Shriver.

17:36.254 --> 17:40.323
Is there a skeleton with a
wig that can drive me home?

17:40.358 --> 17:41.724
I can.

17:41.759 --> 17:43.326
Look at this mess!

17:43.361 --> 17:45.895
Where is the housekeeper?

17:51.204 --> 17:52.635
Well, you already look better.

17:52.637 --> 17:54.103
The doctor should be in any minute.

17:55.874 --> 17:57.206
Chris, what the hell?

17:57.242 --> 18:00.743
There is a room where you can
go in and just get free people.

18:00.778 --> 18:03.312
Yeah, you should give that back.

18:03.348 --> 18:06.149
Look, I'm really sorry I
let you get hurt, Stewie.

18:06.184 --> 18:08.451
I never should've pushed
you into that game.

18:08.486 --> 18:09.852
Oh, it's not your fault.

18:09.888 --> 18:12.421
I just have to accept that I'm not a man

18:12.457 --> 18:14.123
and I'm never going to be one.

18:14.159 --> 18:15.439
That's ridiculous. You can't let

18:15.460 --> 18:18.728
what one woman says in a
grocery store define who you are.

18:18.763 --> 18:20.263
Mom and Dad said it, too.

18:20.298 --> 18:22.565
I heard it through a vent in the wall.

18:22.600 --> 18:24.200
Hey, knock, knock.

18:24.235 --> 18:25.368
Coach Herrera?

18:25.403 --> 18:26.736
You came to see Stewie?

18:26.771 --> 18:29.805
Yeah, I wanted to check in
on this tough little guy.

18:29.841 --> 18:31.674
"Tough little guy"?

18:31.709 --> 18:34.010
It takes a real man to
take a hit like that.

18:34.045 --> 18:36.145
Feel better, sport.

18:36.181 --> 18:37.880
How about that?

18:37.916 --> 18:39.515
"Real man."

18:39.551 --> 18:40.883
See? I told you, Stewie.

18:40.919 --> 18:42.485
You're a big, tough boy.

18:42.520 --> 18:44.287
Yes, I guess I am.

18:44.322 --> 18:45.488
That may be, Stewie.

18:45.523 --> 18:47.790
But if I were you,
I'd stay off the field.

18:47.825 --> 18:50.760
Concussions are the number
one problem in football today.

18:50.795 --> 18:52.828
Recent brain scan studies have shown...

18:54.699 --> 18:58.167
...that brain injuries are
directly linked to dementia

18:58.203 --> 19:00.636
and suicides in former players!

19:00.672 --> 19:02.605
Yet the league...

19:02.640 --> 19:06.642
You can play the music louder
but you can't silence the truth!

19:09.747 --> 19:11.147
Peter, slow down!

19:11.182 --> 19:12.848
No can do, Joe. I'm all hopped up

19:12.884 --> 19:15.351
'cause I Vicks Vapo'd my sack.

19:16.854 --> 19:19.188
I also got some of it in my eyes.

19:20.892 --> 19:23.159
Am I getting them? Am
I getting the robbers?

19:23.194 --> 19:26.329
Peter, put the gun down!

19:26.364 --> 19:28.364
On the floor, punks.

19:28.399 --> 19:29.832
Everybody dies.

19:31.035 --> 19:33.169
My already-irritated eyes!

19:36.949 --> 19:38.941
Aw, damn it, Peter!

19:38.977 --> 19:41.310
This is Officer Swanson,
I need backup at...

19:41.346 --> 19:44.280
Ow! They're beating me
with vaping accessories!

19:44.315 --> 19:46.983
Forget it, there's no time.

19:48.019 --> 19:49.752
Freeze, police!

19:49.787 --> 19:52.255
Too late, Joe. I already
identify with my captors.

19:52.290 --> 19:54.490
Don't hurt Max and Ken.

20:14.212 --> 20:16.946
Holy crap, Joe. That
was freaking amazing!

20:16.981 --> 20:18.214
You kicked their ass!

20:18.249 --> 20:20.383
You're right, I guess I did.

20:20.418 --> 20:21.751
And without my help.

20:21.786 --> 20:23.753
See, this is the Joe I remember.

20:23.788 --> 20:27.256
You know, maybe you
had it in you all along.

20:27.292 --> 20:30.326
Wow. I guess I just
got ground down by years

20:30.361 --> 20:32.528
of people treating
me like an errand boy,

20:32.563 --> 20:35.431
and I just let them walk all over me.

20:35.466 --> 20:37.867
You know, you were a real
pain in the butt as a partner,

20:37.902 --> 20:40.102
but you helped me find myself again.

20:40.138 --> 20:41.537
Thanks, Peter.

20:41.572 --> 20:43.406
You're welcome, Joe.

20:43.441 --> 20:46.642
Excuse me, do you have any
Tab soda I can bring back

20:46.678 --> 20:49.712
to the sex dungeon where I've
been held captive for decades?

20:49.747 --> 20:51.314
Ma'am, this is a crime scene.

20:51.349 --> 20:54.450
I'm gonna have to ask you to move along.

20:54.485 --> 20:57.257
You're right, Peter.
I'm a pretty good cop.

20:57.258 --> 21:58.258
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru